{"name":"Boiling Point","hex":"#d7e9e8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boiling point","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The temperature at which a liquid boils, with the vapor pressure equal to the given external pressure.","The state of being heated, with high aggression."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boiling_point"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boiling Point (1990 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Boiling Point  is a 1990 Japanese crime film written and directed by Takeshi Kitano, who also co-stars under his stage name Beat Takeshi. It was Kitano's second film as a director and first film as a screenwriter. Boiling Point is seen as an important first step in his development as an editor and as a director."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/75/Boiling_Point.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boiling_Point_(1990_film)","wikidata":"Q301823"},{"title":"Boiling Point (1993 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Boiling Point is a 1993 American action thriller film written and directed by James B. Harris and starring Wesley Snipes. The film co-stars Dennis Hopper, Lolita Davidovich, and Viggo Mortensen. It is based on the 1982 novel Money Men by former U.S. Secret Service agent Gerald Petievich."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/ba/Boilingpointpost.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boiling_Point_(1993_film)","wikidata":"Q891030"},{"title":"Boiling Point (2021 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Boiling Point is a 2021 British drama film directed by Philip Barantini and written by Barantini and James Cummings, based on a 2019 short film of the same name. It stars Stephen Graham, Vinette Robinson, Ray Panthaki, and Hannah Walters. It is a one-shot film set in a restaurant kitchen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/18/Boiling_Point_poster.jpg/330px-Boiling_Point_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boiling_Point_(2021_film)","wikidata":"Q109284828"},{"title":"Boiling point","blocks":[{"text":"The boiling point of a substance is the temperature at which the vapor pressure of a liquid equals the pressure surrounding the liquid and the liquid changes into a vapor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/330px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boiling_point","wikidata":"Q1003183"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Boiling_point_vs_molar_mass_graph.png/500px-Boiling_point_vs_molar_mass_graph.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Boiling_point_vs_molar_mass_graph.png/500px-Boiling_point_vs_molar_mass_graph.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boiling points of alkanes, alkenes, ethers, halogenoalkanes, aldehydes, ketones, alcohols and carboxylic acids as a function of molar mass","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoiling_point_vs_molar_mass_graph.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Butane-3D-balls.png/500px-Butane-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Butane-3D-balls.png/500px-Butane-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AButane-3D-balls.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Isobutane-3D-balls.png/500px-Isobutane-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn